{
  "id": 430891313,
  "iid": 22240,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "nettrace_3gpp_32_423: Don't print libxml2 errors on OPEN_NOT_MINE",
  "description": "Suppress any libxml2 errors when trying to open a file as a 3GPP TS 32.423\ntrace format before determining that it is that format (or indeed,\nXML at all.) Prevents console messages to stderr like:\n\nnstrace1.cap:1: parser error : Start tag expected, '<' not found\nG\n^\n\nFor files that are not XML (even if later opened by another wiretap\nfile handler.)\n\n(Eventually we should probably use xmlCtxtSetErrorHandler() with the\nWireshark logging system in other places where libxml2 is used, but\nthat requires libxml2 2.13.0 or later.)",
